egin{bmatrix}x & 2x & 5 \\\\ 3 & x & 4 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$ is $40$, find all the possible values of $x$ **in ascending order**.\n\nIn ascending order, $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}."] [17592186295177 :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point ${S}^{′}$, the image of $S(2,-1)$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${S}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$)$"] [17592186295177 :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a column-vector $x$ containing the coordinates of $S:$\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $x$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $Tx:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Tx & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result, $Tx,$ contains the coordinates of ${S}^{′}.$ Therefore, ${S}^{′}(14,-7).$"] [17592186295178 :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point ${Y}^{′}$, the image of $Y(-2,-3)$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${Y}^{′}($ \n\n$-2$\n\n,\n\n$11$\n\n$)$"] [17592186295178 :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $Y$ under the action of $T$, we first create a column-vector $x$ containing the coordinates of $Y:$\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $x$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $Tx:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Tx & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result, $Tx,$ contains the coordinate