n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(0) & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{2} \\\\ -4{c}_{1}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & =0\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ -8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186391396 :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ 16\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186391397 :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186391398 :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ -8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186391399 :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186391400 :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(